{% extends "quarterly_deep_dive/llm_prompts/base_prompt.j2" %}

{% set output_format_description = "a brief, objective observation (2-3 sentences) focused solely on the primary trend or key finding from the 'Top CWEs in High & Critical CVEs' chart data. No interpretation or recommendations." %}

{% block task_instructions %}
The chart titled '{{ data_context_payload.chart_caption | default('Top CWEs in High & Critical CVEs') }}' (typically a bar chart) displays the most frequent Common Weakness Enumerations (CWEs) found in CVEs rated as High or Critical severity.
Examine the provided data summary for this chart.
Identify and describe the most significant observation. For example:
- Which CWE is most prevalent among high and critical CVEs?
- Are there a few CWEs that dominate, or is the distribution more even?
- How does the frequency of the top CWE compare to others in the list?
Focus only on what the data directly indicates about the frequency of top CWEs in high-risk vulnerabilities.
{% endblock task_instructions %}

{% block data_context %}
Chart ID: {{ data_context_payload.chart_id | default('top_cwe_in_high_risk_cves_chart') }}
Chart Caption: {{ data_context_payload.chart_caption | default('Figure 10. Top CWEs in High & Critical CVEs.') }}

Data Summary:
{{ data_context_payload.chart_data_summary | default("Data not available.") }}
Note: If percentages do not sum to 100%, this may be due to some CVEs lacking an assigned value (i.e., missing or NaN values were excluded from the calculation).
{% endblock data_context %}
